## Why This Is Asked
This assesses practical use of a caching layer in a basic AWS setup, focusing on pattern choice, sizing, TTL, invalidation, and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Cache-aside pattern
- ElastiCache Redis basics (node type, shard, TTL, eviction)
- Integration with EC2 apps and ALB health checks
- Observability with CloudWatch

## Code Example
```java
// Pseudo code for cache-aside
value = cache.get(key);
if (value == null) {
  value = db.query(key);
  cache.set(key, value, ttlSeconds);
}
return value;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle hot keys or write bursts?
- What changes if you switch to DynamoDB with DAX vs Redis?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests disaster recovery readiness, automation capabilities, and cost controls for a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Disaster recovery strategies and RDS cross-region replicas
- Route 53 health checks and failover routing policies
- EC2/ALB endpoint re-routing mechanisms and S3 lifecycle management
- CloudWatch alarms, monitoring, and budget controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-runbook snippet for failover sequencing
async function failover() {
  await promoteReadReplica('secondary-region');
  await updateDNSRecord('secondary-endpoint');
  await verifyReplicaHealth();
  await notifyStakeholders();
}
